{"id": "EUVD-2026-76654", "enisaUuid": "3ff92bff-8da5-390e-935e-51c54418e8df", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nrapidio: mport_cdev: fix use-after-free in dma_req_free()\n\ndma_req_free() acquires buf_mutex through req->map, drops the mapping\nreference with kref_put(), and then dereferences req->map again to unlock\nthe mutex.\n\nIf kref_put() drops the last reference, mport_release_mapping() frees the\nmapping, and the subsequent mutex_unlock() dereferences a freed object. \nThis is a use-after-free.\n\nFix this by caching map and md before kref_put(), clearing req->map while\nholding buf_mutex, and using the cached md for mutex unlocking.\n\nThe bug is reachable from userspace via the RapidIO mport character device\ninterface.", "datePublished": "2026-09-11T19:46:48", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:51:56", "baseScore": 7.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/00c5ed913b0dc563fbeb8a97ea8916c03bbbbf6a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/fc79c07cdcde02c5b17633d78777de6ac2c14b29", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/26ccfe7d69e27b0d933ae0a64a23a0cb9b9a85a6", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/bd8881c24a9520f9c3d3e855d866197f63e471a7", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9a9929ec875ff20922c90c96fd544ae8a2a61a8d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e6e925cc1f8067c65c7bec3da50a0ead3b3ef4e0", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/211c68d817a3d9dc14c0026a59da7cac30f8147e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5cbef379a94b161726c5f504598bf4791d45cedc"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-89742", "GHSA-hcj7-cp6w-gvx9"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.16, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "01765d43-2dfe-3c17-b0be-17b4113774e8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e8de370188d098bb49483c287b44925957c3c9b6 <5cbef379a94b161726c5f504598bf4791d45cedc"}, {"id": "0a4f8819-9fa1-3274-95ab-6ffd559e1e22", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e8de370188d098bb49483c287b44925957c3c9b6 <211c68d817a3d9dc14c0026a59da7cac30f8147e"}, {"id": "5480d1b1-8562-34e1-a3a7-06c0cfdcfbca", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.50"}, {"id": "60422245-a04d-305e-9c0f-00a6f18ee439", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.15.221"}, {"id": "6c890d3c-cb2a-35a8-8656-23ebbba5910a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "709fdc33-8618-3660-ac0d-548f7340321f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e8de370188d098bb49483c287b44925957c3c9b6 <fc79c07cdcde02c5b17633d78777de6ac2c14b29"}, {"id": "78c5dea8-6321-33f2-8f9e-e77416de3c5b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.4"}, {"id": "90ccb162-c848-37e6-8a0d-dee0b32ab69d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e8de370188d098bb49483c287b44925957c3c9b6 <26ccfe7d69e27b0d933ae0a64a23a0cb9b9a85a6"}, {"id": "9c05bec8-ce43-3a74-bb6f-1814a500275b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e8de370188d098bb49483c287b44925957c3c9b6 <9a9929ec875ff20922c90c96fd544ae8a2a61a8d"}, {"id": "a4ea26cb-f435-3ec4-8ae4-b86e41c7f74b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.10.270"}, {"id": "ac96ed3f-9fee-3194-b7ca-4dd1173b4e7f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.109"}, {"id": "b89186a7-e893-3e85-a61d-727fb2e43bae", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e8de370188d098bb49483c287b44925957c3c9b6 <00c5ed913b0dc563fbeb8a97ea8916c03bbbbf6a"}, {"id": "d068638d-b83a-313d-88db-530c4294be7f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "d6e